# Never commit real credentials. set-twilio-credentials.sql holds a live
# Twilio Auth Token in plaintext (audit H4). It is a one-time "run this to
# write the creds into the settings table" file — after running it on the
# server, DELETE it; the secret then lives only in the DB settings table.
# This scoped ignore protects it from `git add -A` even while the repo-root
# .gitignore is absent. Keep it out of every deploy archive as well.
set-twilio-credentials.sql

# Any other local credential drop-ins.
*credentials*.sql
*secret*.sql
